            <div xml:id="d320">

                <pb facs="0446" n="364" xml:id="pg364"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.91265/9: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Italy</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Fletcher</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1925-07-25T13:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">July 25, 1925—1
                                p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>91. Your 119, July 22, 5 p.m. <hi rendition="#italic">Chicago Tribune</hi> has
                    informed Department that it has reason to fear that Mr. George Seldes’ life or
                    physical safety is imperilled in connection with his threatened expulsion or
                    deportation from Rome.</p>
                <p>You should urge the Foreign Office to delay action in the case until a thorough
                    investigation has been made, and express the hope that no violent measures may
                    be resorted to for which the Italian Government might be held responsible.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
